        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0125" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg29"/>

                <head>No. 16.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kirk
                        to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                            Ayres</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-08-14"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August</hi> 14, 1871</date>. (Received September
                        21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 90.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Permit me to say that Mr. Borges, the
                    Brazilian minister, my former colleague, has received the appointment as
                    minister plenipotentiary, &amp;c., to our Government. He is a gentleman of fine
                    ability, and has always expressed the most friendly sentiments toward our
                    country, was a very popular minister here, and, if I am not mistaken, will earn
                    the same reputation at Washington. I therefore have no hesitation in requesting
                    for him a cordial reception.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. C. KIRK.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
